<title>SPAIN: SOCCER-SPAIN BEAT MALTA 4-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-SPAIN BEAT MALTA 4-0 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>ALICANTE, Spain 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain beat Malta 4-0</p>
<p>(halftime 2-0) in a World Cup European group six qualifying</p>
<p>match on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorers - Josep Guardiola 25, Alfonso Perez 40, 46, Juan</p>
<p>Pizzi 90</p>
<p>Teams:</p>
<p>Spain: 1-Andoni Zubizarreta, 2-Armando Alvarez, 3-Agustin</p>
<p>Aranzabal, 4-Abelardo Fernandez, 5-Miguel Angel Nadal,</p>
<p>6-Fernando Hierro (18-Roberto Rios 46th minute), 7-Javier</p>
<p>Manjarin, 8-Luis Enrique, 9-Josep Guardiola (15-Julen Guerrero</p>
<p>75), 10-Raul Gonzalez (16-Juan Pizzi 46), 11-Alfonso Perez.</p>
<p>Malta: 1-Reggie Cini, 2-Lawrence Attard, 3-Richard Buhagiar</p>
<p>(14-Joe Galea 85) 4-Silvia Vella, 5-Jeffrey Chetcuti, 6-Ivan</p>
<p>Zammit (16-Joe Camilleri 78), 7-Gilbert Aguis, 8-Hubert Suda,</p>
<p>9-Noel Turner 10-Joe Brincat 11-Antoine Zahra</p>
<p>    Standings  Pl   W   D   L    F  A   Pts</p>
<p>Spain	     6   5   1   0   19   3   16</p>
<p>Yugoslavia	5   4   0   1   18   4   12</p>
<p>Slovakia	  4   3   0   1   12   5    9</p>
<p>Czech Republic  3   1   1   1    6   1    4</p>
<p>Faroe Islands   5   0   0   5    5  22    0</p>
<p>Malta	     5   0   0   5    0  25    0</p>
<p>Next match: March 31 - Malta v Slovakia.</p>
</text>
